<title>SOUTH KOREA: Soosan Heavy limit down for second day.</title>
<headline>Soosan Heavy limit down for second day.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1997-05-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in South Korea's Soosan Heavy Industries Co fell by their lower limit for the second consecutive session on Monday on rumours, denied by the company, of financial troubles, brokers said.  </p>
<p>Soosan, a specialty vehicle maker, lost 1,200 won, or 7.5 percent, to 14,800 at 0230 GMT.</p>
<p>&quot;The rumours are groundless. We are financially sound,&quot; said a company official.</p>
<p>A Coryo Securities broker said the Soosan rumours had no impact on the market.</p>
<p>-- Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5647</p>
</text>
